{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"fc7208e67b27593d4b31e72bb8020690fb3f42a6c3cddc5a02e607a5170cd8b9","digest":{"component_or_area":"LLM provider configuration and qualification","key_entities":["KNOWN_PROVIDER_NAMES","split_provider_qualifier","_resolve_target","infer_provider","_PROVIDER_QUALIFIER_RE","src/rebar/llm/config.py","src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py","src/rebar/llm/providers.py","ProviderSession._builders","_pydantic_ai_known_providers"],"problem_keywords":["provider qualification","model id parsing","configuration validation","registry membership"],"propositions":["Provider qualification must be decided by membership in a known-provider registry, not by regex shape matching.","A configured provider that is not in the registry should raise LLMConfigError at config-resolution time, not at provider construction.","An unrecognized inline provider prefix in a model string should be treated as unqualified rather than raising an error.","The static frozenset of 24 provider names must exactly match the pydantic-ai runtime registries to prevent silent drift.","The names 'test' and 'google_genai' are not valid provider qualifiers and must not be grandfathered into the set despite existing test pins.","Slashed provider names like 'gateway/openai' must be recognized as valid qualifiers after this change."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787735932300238001,"uuid":"0dc46491-7903-449d-8e63-223756489fc5"}